      "patch": "@@ -165,6 +165,8 @@ guide: |\n   - **Hardware (B300 / NVFP4):** 4× B300 (verified); use `vllm/vllm-openai:latest`\n   - **AMD support:** 8x MI300X / MI325X / MI355X with ROCm 7.2.1 and Python 3.12\n \n+  <!-- overlay:vllm-ascend:huawei_prerequisites -->\n+\n   ### NVIDIA B300: NVFP4 with Eagle3\n \n   ```bash\n@@ -256,6 +258,8 @@ guide: |\n   - Keep vLLM's default block size unless you are tuning long-context\n     throughput; `--block-size 64` is safe to try.\n \n+  <!-- overlay:vllm-ascend:ascend -->\n+\n   ## Client Usage\n \n   Once the vLLM server is running, consume it via the OpenAI-compatible API:\n@@ -290,7 +294,7 @@ guide: |\n \n   start = time.time()\n   response = client.chat.completions.create(\n-      model=\"moonshotai/Kimi-K2.6\",\n+      model={{client_model}},\n       messages=messages,\n       max_tokens=2048\n   )\n@@ -318,3 +322,5 @@ guide: |\n   - [vLLM multimodal inputs guide](https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/features/multimodal_inputs.html)\n   - [vLLM Expert Parallelism docs](https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/serving/expert_parallel_deployment.html)\n   - [vLLM NixlConnector usage guide](https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/features/nixl_connector_usage.html)\n+\n+  <!-- overlay:vllm-ascend:ascend_references -->",
